{# Advisory template — human-readable Markdown form.
   Rendered by the publish_advisory step of playbook.cra_cvd@v1 alongside
   the machine-readable CSAF 2.0 emission in advisory.csaf2.json.j2. Both
   are published at the coordinated disclosure date
   __disclosure_target_date__.

   Fields:
     advisory_id         : operator-issued advisory id (e.g. OP-2026-0007).
     cve_id              : CVE identifier when a CNA has assigned one;
                           empty when no CVE has been assigned.
     title               : one-line summary of the vulnerability.
     summary             : 1–3 sentence executive summary.
     affected_products   : list of {product, affected_versions,
                                    fixed_version_or_workaround} rows.
     severity_display    : CVSS v4.0 vector plus qualitative label
                           (LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / CRITICAL).
     impact              : what an unpatched instance is exposed to.
     mitigations         : temporary mitigations for operators who
                           cannot immediately deploy the fix.
     fix_reference       : release id / build id the fix ships in.
     credit_display      : reporter credit line when the reporter has
                           opted in via the reporter-credit consent
                           capture on the coordinate_disclosure step;
                           the string "reporter chose to remain
                           anonymous" when they have not.
     disclosure_date_iso : ISO 8601 date the advisory becomes public.
     advisory_url        : canonical URL of the operator's advisory
                           listing.
     operator_display    : operator name as published in the CVD policy.
#}
# {{ operator_display }} security advisory {{ advisory_id }}{% if cve_id %} — {{ cve_id }}{% endif %}

Published: {{ disclosure_date_iso }}
Canonical: {{ advisory_url }}

## Title

{{ title }}

## Summary

{{ summary }}

## Affected products

{% for row in affected_products -%}
- **{{ row.product }}** — versions {{ row.affected_versions }}
  Fix: {{ row.fixed_version_or_workaround }}
{% endfor %}

## Severity

{{ severity_display }}

## Impact

{{ impact }}

## Mitigations

{% if mitigations -%}
{% for m in mitigations -%}
- {{ m }}
{% endfor -%}
{% else -%}
None documented beyond deploying the fix.
{%- endif %}

## Fix

{{ fix_reference }}

## Credit

{{ credit_display }}

## Coordinated disclosure

This advisory was published under the operator's coordinated
vulnerability disclosure policy. Case handling follows the CRA
Article 14 lifecycle and ISO/IEC 29147 / 30111 disciplines.
